  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1218 AM CDT Fri Apr 17 2026\n\nRain chances continue Saturday night but begin to shift south as \nsurface high pressure briefly moves over the area Sunday morning \nbefore moving east Sunday afternoon. This will leave low to medium \nrain chances primarily in the southern and western-most portions of \nthe area Sunday during the day, with mainly cool and cloudy \nconditions in store. Breezy north to east wind continues into Sunday \nmorning before easing Sunday afternoon and evening. Though mid-level \nridging builds over the area Sunday, a disturbance within the \nsouthwesterly flow will likely generate showers and thunderstorms \nwest of the area Sunday night which will shift east across our area \ninto Tuesday. The cloudy and cooler conditions continue during this \ntime, though wind will be lighter than the weekend. \n\nWe'll start to see the return of southeasterly flow Tuesday which \nlooks to continue for the rest of the long term period. This will \nbring a day by day warming trend back to the area with highs \nreturning into the 80s mid-week. Weak mid-level ridging remains over \nthe area mid to late week keeping precipitation chances low, but \ndisturbances aloft and a dryline in West Texas keep rain chances non-\nzero.",
